                "entry_id": "e1866a59-32ab-358f-9d03-983b45f625a0",
                "word": "cardhouse",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "18691241-8f72-41cb-9aa4-cf76ad7c6b1a",
                        "entry_id": "e1866a59-32ab-358f-9d03-983b45f625a0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cardhouses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10d708d1-80ac-3d8f-b6de-74df03c69b24",
                        "entry_id": "e1866a59-32ab-358f-9d03-983b45f625a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A business establishment that hosts card-playing, especially one where patrons play poker."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4364ed44-9dc5-4515-86cb-7ef526bf5e4f",
                                "sense_id": "10d708d1-80ac-3d8f-b6de-74df03c69b24",
                                "text": "\"Twas first to the cardhouse and then down to Maisie's,\" intoned that mournful ballad \"The Cowboy's Lament.\" But most real-life trail riders went first to the bathtub and then to the haberdasher, if only because neither Maisie nor the cardhouse would truly welcome a man so long as he had the look and smell of a summer in the saddle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80bc9fc7-d87c-4353-a8fe-992ea5d5cba2",
                                "sense_id": "10d708d1-80ac-3d8f-b6de-74df03c69b24",
                                "text": "He spends six nights a week at the cardhouse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb53a449-d368-45d8-952f-dcae6687a8b5",
                                "sense_id": "10d708d1-80ac-3d8f-b6de-74df03c69b24",
                                "text": "Caro's Law of Tells One of the first experts to describe Stage 3—poker players as actors—was Mike Caro, a specialist in draw poker as played in the cardhouses of Gardena, California."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eaf91b05-f346-3de5-817e-fe3b93749989",
                        "entry_id": "e1866a59-32ab-358f-9d03-983b45f625a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A structure of plate-like mineral deposits that rest on each other's edges."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "afda7c5c-609d-4d6c-8fdc-8e065ce1169d",
                                "sense_id": "eaf91b05-f346-3de5-817e-fe3b93749989",
                                "text": "He also expressed the opinion that certain sensitive clays derived their properties from the fact that the flaky minerals were arranged in an unstable “cardhouse” fabric."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96db0eaa-f347-421e-80d7-4557037307d2",
                                "sense_id": "eaf91b05-f346-3de5-817e-fe3b93749989",
                                "text": "The microstructures do not appear to conform entirely to either cardhouse or honeycomb structures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c5ba702-1fc4-4bb1-a81d-9f49fc8eab89",
                                "sense_id": "eaf91b05-f346-3de5-817e-fe3b93749989",
                                "text": "The Champlain clays are believed to have a somewhat special arrangement of the individual soil particles such that the plate-like particles are oriented to each other in an edge to face arrangement in the undisturbed condition, i.e. \"cardhouse\" structure."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d68a6637-fe83-3b6b-8043-c7b8d21d0822",
                        "entry_id": "e1866a59-32ab-358f-9d03-983b45f625a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of house of cards (any sense)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecc9ccb4-93dd-475e-b66e-2a7f17e89f0b",
                                "sense_id": "d68a6637-fe83-3b6b-8043-c7b8d21d0822",
                                "text": "The photographer glanced up at them over a four-storeyed cardhouse, which he had built out of crispbread."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfb43720-67d1-40ef-9bb0-9a05fab4a885",
                                "sense_id": "d68a6637-fe83-3b6b-8043-c7b8d21d0822",
                                "text": "On the other hand (and perhaps incompatibly) he was thought to be dangerously addicted to speculation: 'an inveterate theorist, an intellectual cardhouse builder'."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f352c558-0746-46d8-86fc-836c3aa74d93",
                                "sense_id": "d68a6637-fe83-3b6b-8043-c7b8d21d0822",
                                "text": "Many of my earliest memories are mysteries I probably will never solve now that those who might have explained them to me are gone. I fall back on experience and intuition, build my fragile cardhouse of speculation, and hope my solutions are not ridiculously far from the mark."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
